{"event_type":"review","id":"d2d77f62d993dfcd30a7379e9a6646742072375ccf262ba68d6aa2fea748b798","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T19:52:06Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/83855f32ca8809b3cce5e4ba208e77e7047f13e1226c99deb3b66580c89c8ee7","sha256":"83855f32ca8809b3cce5e4ba208e77e7047f13e1226c99deb3b66580c89c8ee7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/08a08a9b7a70da35f122ed01af5bbd6b8b28723ea54428f7bdbffb3281af507d","sha256":"08a08a9b7a70da35f122ed01af5bbd6b8b28723ea54428f7bdbffb3281af507d"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dac5ce5b1c765e5e9291bb79a547b77b46245002166d2d27675f6a936f608c47","sha256":"dac5ce5b1c765e5e9291bb79a547b77b46245002166d2d27675f6a936f608c47"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/92d99a019d24f2fd6218858ff1e6d80780caf7575030b3a421bcf1fbcc2911b7","sha256":"92d99a019d24f2fd6218858ff1e6d80780caf7575030b3a421bcf1fbcc2911b7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2484db03c1d64ebfac83dbbc13cfc3d35b26ea23f90ee6d8f10866337b11e901","sha256":"2484db03c1d64ebfac83dbbc13cfc3d35b26ea23f90ee6d8f10866337b11e901"}],"attempt_id":"f624b8435e89371962412957a1580f7bb8005219a9e4ebfece88fa07e123cab8:0:1","base":"d56ae000c08368630cf9135f752417e40ee52393","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"aea46a5bf75ded202d97da61a31dcd338df283e8","body":"**Append each absent key once, using its final value.**\n\n`object.has(key)` checks only the input object, and the loop never adds entries to it. Repeated updates to an absent key therefore append one entry per update. `JsonObject` is not Map-like. Its constructor keeps the supplied array, and `get` returns the first matching entry. For an empty object and updates `[[\"a\", 1], [\"a\", 2]]`, the result is `[[\"a\", 1], [\"a\", 2]]` and `get(\"a\")` returns `1`. The file header states last-write-wins for `setKeys`, so this violates that contract.\n\nIterate over `replacement` instead. `Map` keeps each key at its first insertion position and holds its final value. Each absent key is then appended once, with its last update.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  for (const [key, value] of updates) {\n+  for (const [key, value] of replacement) {\n     if (!object.has(key)) entries.push([key, value]);\n   }\n```\n\n</details>","id":"870bee2c7b1f048c89dda5d126ac29f9c04ed0abd1ed249b71bdc1861a78e290","intervals":[[18,18]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/publishJsonEdit.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Append each absent key once, using its final value."}],"head":"681501735a408b5af8669c284ae08e4e6e6c0ece","head_tree":"ff441c47f135816927d2c105b0555b66502df3d8","input_scope":[{"blob":"aea46a5bf75ded202d97da61a31dcd338df283e8","intervals":[[1,30]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/publishJsonEdit.ts"}],"job_id":"f624b8435e89371962412957a1580f7bb8005219a9e4ebfece88fa07e123cab8:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"aea46a5bf75ded202d97da61a31dcd338df283e8","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/crq/internal/publishJsonEdit.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"aea46a5bf75ded202d97da61a31dcd338df283e8","intervals":[[1,30]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/publishJsonEdit.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"aea46a5bf75ded202d97da61a31dcd338df283e8","intervals":[[1,30]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/publishJsonEdit.ts"}],"scope_digest":"3c4463eaad9bcdd93452db255059e95d9c756c69898610eb3aa2f3674dafcc26","source":{"authenticated":true,"id":"backfill-f624b8435e89371962412957a1580f7bb8005219a9e4ebfece88fa07e123cab8-g0-20261115T195017Z","prod